Version-0.2.27+gtk4 (GTK 4 port)

	* Ported to GTK 4, built with Meson.
	* Removed the support for Susie plugins.
	* Removed lib/dllloader.
	* The system libexif and GLib replace the bundled libexif and MD5 code.
	* New loaders for Sun raster, WBMP, PNM, XPM, ZIM (KID98, PC-9801),
	  Pi (PC-9801, X68000; 16 and 256 colours), PIC (X68000, FM TOWNS,
	  PC-88VA), PIC2 (X68000), MAKI01 (.mki, before MAG), MB (PC-8801), MB2 (PC-9801)
	  and AK5/MSL (MASL,
	  PC-9801; an .msl is played by its scenario, with its PCM
	  sound through GStreamer); formats of the
	  installed gdk-pixbuf loaders (WebP, AVIF, HEIF, JPEG XL, ...) are
	  recognized, and formats nothing can read are not listed.
	* Comments on the thumbnail view: "Subject" and "Comment" columns in
	  the detail view, a tooltip in the album view.
	* Comment editor window: Close button (and Esc).
	* Corrected spelling and wording of the English messages and menus
	  (Faild -> Failed, Buttton, Thumnail, Tool -> Tools, ...); old key
	  bindings in ~/.gimv/keyaccelrc for renamed menu items are migrated.
	  po/gimageview.pot regenerated (tools/po-update.py).
	* Dialog buttons (OK, Cancel, Apply, ...) are translated again.
	* Help > Document shows the (Japanese) documents in other locales too.
	* View > Layout and Window Composition show pictures of the layouts
	  (a row of icon buttons; name and shortcut in the tooltip).
	* New GStreamer movie plugin: plays movies and audio in the image view
	  (the formats depend on the installed GStreamer plugins) and makes
	  movie thumbnails.  It is the default player when no default view
	  mode for movies is set.
	* Archives are read with libarchive instead of running lha, unzip, rar
	  and tar; 7z, tar.xz and tar.zst are supported too, Shift_JIS and
	  EUC-JP file names in old zip/lha archives are converted.  The -lh1- method of
	  LHarc 1.x, which libarchive does not read, is unpacked by gimv, and
	  LZH archives with names not in UTF-8 are read.  With liblhasa, LZH
	  archives are read with all the old methods (-lh4-, -lzs-, -lz5-,
	  -pm1-, ...) and self-extracting ones (MS-DOS, X68000, ...) too.
	* File names not in the charset of the system (Shift_JIS names of the
	  MS-DOS days, EUC-JP of UNIX) are guessed in a Japanese environment;
	  bytes that cannot be read are shown as %XX.  Guessed names are in
	  italics, and [Edit | File Names to UTF-8...] renames them to UTF-8.
	* Buttons use the icons of the desktop icon theme (Preferences >
	  Common > Appearance); icon sets (iconset= in gimvrc, ~/.gimv/icons/<name>)
	  may contain PNG and SVG files.
	* Tools > Set as Wallpaper sets the selected image as the desktop
	  wallpaper (Xfce, GNOME, KDE Plasma, MATE, Cinnamon, LXDE/LXQt, feh;
	  "This Desktop" picks the running one).  Other formats and images in
	  archives are converted to PNG in ~/.gimv/wallpaper.
	* The movie player shows the elapsed and the total time; a click on a
	  playing movie no longer moves on to the next file.
	* Top-down BMP and CMYK JPEG files are loaded.
	* Printing (GTK print dialog): File > Print... (Ctrl+P) in the image
	  window and the thumbnail window (selected images, one per page), and
	  Print... in the popup menus.  The "Image" tab of the print dialog
	  chooses fit to the page or a resolution in dpi, turning the image to
	  the page orientation, and printing the file name.
	* Movie seek bar: pointing at it shows the frame and the time there
	  (GStreamer player; the time only for audio).
	* Transparent images are shown over a checkerboard (View >
	  Checkerboard Behind Transparency, also in the popup menu and in
	  Preferences > Image Window > Background); off blends them with the
	  background colour as before.
	* Preferences > Movie and Audio: continuous play on/off.
	* Preferences > Movie and Audio: optionally ignore mouse actions for
	  next/previous image, zoom, rotation and scrolling while a movie or
	  audio file plays (off by default: the mouse settings apply).
	* Thumbnail view: directory names end with "/" in all view modes.
	* Movies and audio files in archives can be played (they are extracted
	  first; before, the player reported "Resource not found").
	* Detail view: the image size is read from the file header (formats
	  of gdk-pixbuf, and JPEG) instead of "Unknown" until the image was
	  loaded; it is also updated when an image is opened.  The sizes are
	  read in the background after the list is shown.
	* The rotation of each image is remembered (kept in its comment file
	  under ~/.gimv/comment, hidden in the comment editor) and restored
	  when it is opened again; Preferences > Image Window > Image.
	* The HTML manual (Japanese) has screenshots, and its descriptions of
	  the menus, toolbars, mouse menus, preferences and key bindings were
	  changed to match this version.
	* The same files in different folders: the indexer hashes the images
	  of the same size as another one after the rest (stage 4, "Look for
	  the same files" in [Preferences | Index]; hours the first time, in
	  directory order, the same names first), and [Tools | Find
	  Duplicates in the Index...], "Find Duplicates with the Folders in
	  It..." (directory view) and "Find the Same Files" (thumbnail view)
	  show them at once.  The index database is version 6.
	* Find Duplicates: "Move All Marked to Trash..." for every group; each
	  file is compared with the one kept again before it is moved; the
	  comments (tags) and bookmarks of the deleted ones can go to the
	  image kept; or "Trash and Leave Links" keeps the names, as links to
	  the image kept (hard links, symbolic links across file systems).
	* Find Duplicates: the similar ones are compared again (small, then
	  at full size) and sorted into Same Pixels, Saved Again, Brightness,
	  Colours, Partly Different and Alike, Other Pictures; the groups
	  are listed under headings of their kinds that fold (the last three
	  folded at first).  Same Pixels and Saved Again show the one
	  suggested to keep and why (the most metadata, PNG over JPEG, the
	  most pixels, the highest JPEG quality, guessed from its tables),
	  without marking any to delete.
	* The indexer keeps a file moved away and replaced at once (in the
	  same batch of events) instead of dropping it.
	* Update All Thumbnails works like loading: the thumbnails on the
	  screen are made first (the scroll position is kept), the rest in the
	  background without keeping them in memory; the progress (n/N) is
	  shown and the stop button stops it.  The preference "GUI redraw
	  interval while loading" is gone (and the tip about it).
	* Detail view: the title of the column the list is sorted by shows the
	  arrow (it was lost with every sort and only stayed on columns that
	  sort nothing); "Image size" sorts by the area; columns with no sort
	  are not clickable.
	* The thumbnail size in the toolbar can be typed in (all the keys were
	  taken from it); Enter takes the size and gives the keys back to the
	  window (Shift+R, Ctrl+R).
	* The editing keys of a text field (Ctrl+A, Ctrl+C, Ctrl+X, Ctrl+V,
	  Ctrl+Z, ...) go to the text field the focus is in, not to the menu
	  keys of the window (Ctrl+A selected all the thumbnails while the
	  location or the thumbnail size was being edited).
	* Detail view: Ctrl+A and Ctrl+N (Select All, Unselect All) work with
	  the focus in the list; the list took Ctrl+A for itself and did
	  nothing.
	* Detail view: no "cb_sorter_changed: assertion" message on quit after
	  sorting.
	* Open the Folder (from a collection) shows the image chosen also when
	  the folder was not open yet (it showed the top of the folder).
	* Detail view: switching tabs (closing one too) keeps where the list of
	  the tab was scrolled to (it went to the top).
	  The cursor (for the cursor keys) is put back on the image it was on
	  if that is on screen, on the first image on screen otherwise (it
	  was on the first image of the list).
	* Tabs of the thumbnails in a narrow place: the current tab keeps a
	  width its name can be read in, the others a few characters (all were
	  "..."); the close button is on the current tab only, the middle
	  button closes any tab; the current tab is lighter.  "Show full path"
	  is off by default (the name of the folder; the full path in the
	  tooltip either way).
	* Movie player: a mute button and a volume slider at the right end of
	  the control bar (GStreamer, MPlayer); the same for all the windows,
	  kept in gimvrc (imgview_movie_volume, imgview_movie_mute).
	* Songs (m4a, mp3, flac, ogg, ...): the album art in the tags is shown
	  while the song plays, and is its thumbnail (GStreamer).
	* The "Data" tab shows the information of a song or a movie: title,
	  artist, album, album artist, composer, track, disc, date, genre,
	  comment, length, the formats of the sound and the picture
	  (GStreamer's discoverer, in a thread; shown only, in italics).
	* The album art is shown at its own size (it was stretched over the
	  place, coarse), smaller only when the place is smaller; the zoom of
	  images (zoom in / out, the percentages, fit) changes its size.
	* The seek bar of movies goes to the end: it stopped at 99 % (a page
	  size of 1), so the time at the end was short of the length
	  (03:11 / 03:13) and the last 1 % could not be seeked to.
	* Text viewer (plain text documents): a horizontal scroll bar for long
	  lines (they could be read only by moving the cursor).
	* "Save Smaller..." in the right button menu of the thumbnails saves
	  the selected images smaller (800 px of height or less by default)
	  as new files (big_resized.jpg next to big.jpg), in a thread; it can
	  keep the EXIF without the GPS and copy the comments, and never
	  overwrites.
	* "Crop Image..." (C) in the image window and the right button menus
	  of the image: a frame on the image (moved, resized, drawn anew),
	  the ratio, "Detect the Edges" (the border of the color of the edges
	  taken off: a small thing scanned on white), saved as name_crop.jpg
	  next to the image (Enter; Esc stops), in threads.
	* Album modes: Ctrl+F finds a thumbnail by its file name, as the
	  detail view.
	* Detail view: the widths of the columns are kept (after a rename, a
	  sort, a refresh; in other tabs; the next time).
	* Rename: the name without the extension is edited, the extension
	  stays; "Change the extension too" edits it all, and a name without
	  the extension of an image is asked about.
	* "Join Images..." in the right button menu of the thumbnails: the
	  selected images one below another, side by side or in a grid, the
	  same width (height) or not, saved as name_join.jpg next to the
	  first one; the overlaps of the pieces of one photo are looked for
	  and can be put right, the seam shown near its size (also as the
	  difference), in threads.
	* Faces: the model files are checked (SHA-256); a broken download or
	  another file of the same name is not used, and the preferences tell
	  which one to download again.  The index records the model the
	  features of the faces were made with; with another one (a new
	  version), the features are made again at the place of each face,
	  the faces and their names kept.  "meson test faces" runs the models
	  when they are there.
	* Duplicate images: in an Other Sizes group, a copy that is a smaller
	  one only made larger (twice or more; predicted from the small one by
	  a fitted enlarging) shows "Looks like an enlarged copy" and is not
	  the one kept; looked for in a thread after the groups are shown.
	* Manual: the Tips are brought up to date (tips about the bars and the
	  window size of the image window that no longer apply are removed;
	  the memory buffer, the thumbnail size, the custom layout).
	* The HTML manual has a chapter "What Do You Want to Do?" that finds
	  the way from what one wants to do (tagging several images at once,
	  finding the images of a person, ...).
	* Mouse button preferences: the side buttons "back" (button 8) and
	  "forward" (button 9) can be assigned (nothing by default).
	* English manual (HTML) and English plain text documents in the Help
	  menu; they are shown for every language that has no documents of its
	  own (only Japanese has).
	* Color scheme (Preferences > Common > Appearance): the desktop theme,
	  light or dark.  With the desktop theme, a dark theme that GTK 4
	  cannot read (no gtk-4.0 directory, e.g. Greybird-dark) is shown with
	  the dark Adwaita.  Icons of GImageView drawn only with black lines
	  are drawn with light lines in dark colors.
	* File open dialog: "Thumbnails of the selected files" also opens the
	  selected folders, each in a tab of its own.
	* Image index (SQLite): gimv-indexer keeps the dates and tags of the
	  images of the directories given in Preferences > Index, in the
	  background.  The "Date" and "Tag" tabs of the side notebook open
	  them in a result tab; tags are edited from the thumbnail view and
	  kept in the comment files, renamed and merged with F2; automatic
	  tags (folder, camera, shape); desktop notices of new images; Tools >
	  Missing Images... for the comments of images that went missing.
	* Faces and people (OpenCV 4.8, YuNet and SFace models): gimv-faces
	  finds faces and groups them; the "People" tab, the faces window
	  (naming, guesses, unnamed groups, tags of people) and the faces
	  panel of the image view (P), where a face can also be added by hand.
	  The names are kept in the comment files as "person/NAME" tags.
	* Tools > Search Images...: images of the index by tags and names
	  (and, not), by the date taken, narrowed by the tags of the images
	  found; searches can be kept by name.
	* Thumbnails: the freedesktop.org cache (~/.cache/thumbnails) is read
	  and written; thumbnails are made in worker threads, from the EXIF
	  thumbnail of a JPEG when it is big enough; they are turned and
	  flipped by the EXIF orientation and by the rotation and flip the
	  user gave the image.
	* Lists: Ctrl+F searches the rows (directory view, detail view, Data
	  tab, preferences, index tabs, ...).
	* Status bar: the path, position and size of the focused image, or
	  the number and total size of the images selected.
	* Data tab: the comments written in the image file itself (JPEG, PNG,
	  GIF, MAG) are shown in italics, and the tags of the image.
	* Image view: Copy the Image to the Clipboard (Shift+Ctrl+C), Flip
	  Horizontally (X, remembered with the rotation), Open the Folder.
	* Two pages: the preview and the image window show two pages side by
	  side ([Two Pages] of the right button menu, T; right to left or left
	  to right, the first page alone, shift by one page with O).  The
	  status bar tells the pages shown ("Two Pages 2-3 / 8"); the image
	  window has a Two Pages button, with its menu under the arrow.
	  Layouts of pages: pages side by side x rows (up to 4 x 3), right to
	  left, the first page alone, under a name; Two Pages (2 x 1) and Four
	  Pages (2 x 2) at first, [Two Pages | Edit Layouts...] for more.
	  With "Auto resize to image size" the image window is sized for all
	  the pages of the layout, once, not at each page.
	* A book read with pages side by side goes on from its last page when
	  its tab is opened again (~/.gimv/books); the pages of the next turn
	  are read beforehand in a thread.
	* MAG files whose user name ends early with 0x1a (no comment; some
	  saved on the X68000) are shown (only the "Data" tab was, with the
	  header taken as the name).
	* A loader for PIC2 (.p2, X68000; up to 24 bits, all four kinds of
	  blocks, several blocks in one file); its author, title, comment and
	  saver are shown in the "Data" tab.
	* A tab of a folder comes back where it was scrolled, after the tab of
	  an archive opened from it is closed (it showed its top).
	* The comments of Pi and PIC files (and their machine) are shown in the
	  "Data" tab.
	* Fixed: closing the tab of an archive while its thumbnails were made
	  could crash, and a page chosen while they were made was not shown
	  (the preview stayed on the image before).
	* [Join Images] reads MAG, Pi and the other formats of gimv's own
	  loaders too (saved as PNG).  A PNG joined or cropped takes the
	  comments written in the files.
	* Pages side by side: the side of the image under the pointer shows
	  where a click goes ("◀ Next", "Previous ▶").
	* A comment written in the image file: its first 4 lines in the list
	  of the "Data" tab, and, selected, the whole with its lines.
	* MAG, ZIM, Pi, PIC and MAKI images are shown with the pixels of their
	  machine (the PC-9801 1.2 high, the X68000 512 dots wide 4/3 wide).
	* The images of a date are opened newest first, with the arrow of the
	  date taken in the detail view (a sort chosen in the menu or a title
	  of the detail view sorts them so; the one already chosen too).
	* The status bar: the label of two pages at the right (not moved by
	  the index status before it); the empty progress bar not drawn.
	* Pages side by side are for the tab (the book) they were turned on in
	  only: images of other tabs, dates or tags are shown alone.
	* Fixed a crash closing the tab of an archive with the same name twice
	  in it (or opened again while an image of it was still held).
	* The thumbnails of folders and archives are their covers (the first
	  image by name), looked for in threads, within 3 s and 256 MB
	  unpacked for archives that cannot be listed (rar, 7z, tar.gz).
	* Sort by name: numbers in names by their value (0p.jpg, 1.jpg,
	  2.jpg, 10.jpg), [View | Sort File List | Numbers by Value] to turn it
	  off.  Clicking a column title of the detail view keeps the other
	  sort options.
	* Bookmarks of images (~/.gimv/bookmarks), in the index or not:
	  [Edit | Bookmark...] and the right button menus (no key by default,
	  one can be given in ~/.gimv/keyaccelrc), an optional note, the
	  "Bookmarks" tab (by the day added, with or without a note), the
	  note in the tooltip; they follow the images moved or renamed.
	* Edit Tags: an entry with the tags below it (× takes one away),
	  the tags in use to click, the names of people kept; also in
	  [Edit | Edit Tags...] and the right button menus of the preview
	  and the image window.
	* The tags of the Data tab and of Edit Tags are laid out as words
	  (no columns with wide gaps).  A row of the Data tab that is not one
	  of the keys to edit there (X-IMG-Tags, a comment of the file) shows
	  its own key and is only shown.  A line break in a tag or a value
	  (a pasted text) becomes a space.
	* The index dates an image by the "Date" of its comment first (images
	  of SNS have no EXIF and names that are not dates): "2025-04-01",
	  "2025/4/1 10:15", "2025年4月1日 10時15分", ...
	* "Date taken" column of the detail view and View > Sort File List > by
	  Date Taken: the date of the index (comment, EXIF, file name,
	  modification time); the modification time outside the index.
	* After a sort (or a change of the display mode) the thumbnails
	  loaded first are the ones now at the top, not the ones that were.
	* Data tab: a value typed and saved with "Save" (not Enter) is kept,
	  under the key the combo shows (it may show one it never said it
	  had chosen), and the entry shows its value from the start.  The
	  keys to fill in (Subject, Date, ...) are shown for an image with a
	  comment file too, empty keys are not written.
	* Properties: the name and the type (file(1)) cut when long, so the
	  dialog stays on the screen, and selectable; "Copy" puts the full
	  path on the clipboard.  "Copy Path" in the right button menu of
	  the thumbnails.
	* Keywords that were UTF-8 read as Shift_JIS (Windows Photo Gallery)
	  are put right, or left out when they cannot be; IPTC keywords of
	  a record are read in one charset.
	* The keywords other programs put (XMP dc:subject, IPTC Keywords, the
	  sidecar files "x.jpg.xmp" and "x.xmp", followed while watching):
	  kept apart in the index (an automatic kind that can be turned off),
	  shown and looked for with the tags put by hand: a keyword and a tag of the same name are one tag
	  in the Tag tab, the Data tab, the search window and Edit Tags.
	* The index reads EXIF, XMP and IPTC with gexiv2 (Exiv2) when built
	  with it: the date, the camera and the keywords of HEIF, PNG, WebP,
	  TIFF and raw files too, not of JPEG only.
	* EXIF of the formats other than JPEG (TIFF, raw, PNG, WebP, HEIF,
	  JPEG XL, ...) with gexiv2: Show EXIF Data... shows it, the images
	  and the thumbnails are turned by its orientation (not again for
	  HEIF/AVIF and JPEG XL, which their decoders turn, nor for TIFF,
	  which libtiff turns over in part: the rest gdk-pixbuf gives).
	* "Scan EXIF Data..." is "Show EXIF Data..." (it shows them).
	* Find Duplicates rewritten for comparing and deleting: one search
	  sorts the duplicates into Identical (md5 of the files of the same
	  size), Other Sizes (the same shape) and Similar; the result window
	  has the groups on the left and their images side by side on the
	  right (size, file size, format, date taken, how alike, folder,
	  comment), each to keep or to delete (suggested for the identical and
	  resized ones), and moves the ones to delete of a group to the trash
	  (a group at a time, after asking).  The search
	  runs in a thread and reads the pictures itself (not the thumbnails
	  loaded); the comparison methods of the submenu are gone.
	* File > Save Image... [Ctrl+S] of the image window (and Save Image
	  As... of the preview): the image shown, in its full size and turned
	  as shown, saved as JPEG, PNG, WebP, AVIF, TIFF, BMP or PNM (a HEIC
	  as a JPEG, ...) with the quality chosen, in a thread; with gexiv2
	  the EXIF, XMP and IPTC of the file are copied (the orientation put
	  to normal).  A new image saver plugin (gdk-pixbuf) writes JPEG,
	  WebP, AVIF, TIFF, BMP and ICO; savers take options ("quality").
	* Tags are a tree by "/" ("Travel/Kyoto" below "Travel") in the tag
	  tab: a parent counts and opens the images of the tags below it
	  (the search window too), is there even when not put on an image,
	  and renaming it renames the tags below it.
	* The Data tab shows a tag with levels part by part ("Travel / Kyoto"),
	  a parent part opening the images of the tags below it.  In Edit
	  Tags the parents are dimmed, and a parent in "Tags in Use" types
	  "Travel/" to pick from the tags below it.
	* A tag dragged onto another in the tag tab is moved below it or
	  merged into it (asked in a popover; a merge is confirmed), or moved
	  to the top when dropped on the "Tag" row.  A click opens a tag when
	  the button is released, not when it is pressed.
	* The tags of the search window make a tree as in the tag tab: a
	  parent (shown even when not put on an image) counts the tags below
	  it, opens with its arrow, and as a condition brings the tags below
	  it to the top.  Typing finds the last part of a name, its parents
	  opened.
	* The tags of people are a tree by "/" too ("Family/Parents"): in the
	  tag tab (parents count and open the tags below them, renaming and
	  dragging move the tags below along), the people tab, the search
	  window, the data tab and the dialog of the tags of a person.
	* "Edit Tags with the Folders in It..." of the directory view: the
	  tags of all the images of a folder and the folders below it (looked
	  for in a thread).  Writing many tags shows its progress and can be
	  stopped.
	* The tabs showing a tag (or a tag below it) take its new name when
	  the tag is renamed, moved or merged.
	* [Edit | Keyboard Shortcuts...]: the keys of the menus of both
	  windows and the other keys of keyconf, changed by pressing the new
	  key, at once and kept; a key of another item of the same window is
	  asked about, and the defaults can be brought back.
	* Context menus open to the right of the pointer: a long one slides
	  up instead of getting scroll bars.
	* Keywords that Photoshop on a Mac wrote as Shift_JIS read as Mac
	  Roman ("éëóøÅié ê^" for "資料（写真") are put right; the images
	  with keywords are read again once.
	* Data tab: "Remove Item" removes the item selected; "Delete
	  Comment..." (was "Delete", which removed the whole comment file at
	  once) asks first and keeps the tags.  The index reads the tags of a
	  comment saved or deleted at once.
	* Scrollbars are always shown (a preference, on by default).
	* GtkTreeView and the other API deprecated in GTK 4.10 are no longer
	  used (GtkListView / GtkColumnView); GTK 4.12 and GLib 2.72 are
	  required.

Version-0.2.27

	* Added some options for slideshow.
	  (Thanks! > Christian Hammers <lathspell@users.sourceforge.net>)
	* Added Xine image loader for movie thumbnail. (experimental)
	* The bug that sometime same files are appeared numbers of times on
	  same thumbnail view has been fixed.
	  (Thanks reporting > shlomif)
	* Enable to open archived files which has "[" in its filename.
	* Other minor bug fixes are made.

Version-0.2.26

	* Improved performance of redrawing thumbnail view.
	* Improved preference of "fit image size to window" feature.
	  (Thanks! > Brent Baccala <baccala@users.sourceforge.net>)
	* Fixed bugs on 64bit envirponment.
	  (Thanks! > Tomoya TAKA <tomoya@olive.plala.or.jp>)
	* Enabled to open EXIF view from image window.
	* Added image scale preferences for slideshow.
	* Removed obsolete summary modes of thumbnail view.
	  ("List" and "Thumbnail" mode)
	* Fixed compile time error on Gtk+-2.4
	* Other minor fixes and improvements.

Version-0.2.25

	* Adapt to latest MPlayer.
	* Xienerama support.
	* "270" orientation label is changed to "-90".
	* Some minor usabilty fix of comment view.

Version-0.2.24

	* "Auto fit without zoom in" feature has been fixed.
	* Added "Fit width" and "Fit height" feature.
	* The bug that sometimes mplayer fails to start playing has been fixed.
	* Fixed double freeing bug of JPEG loader.
	  (Thanks! > sheepman <sheepman@tcn.zaq.ne.jp>)
	* Fixed a bug in DnD support
	  (Thanks! > MINAMI Hirokazu <h_minami@users.sourceforge.net>)
	* Remove trailing slash when create directory.
	  (Thanks! > Douglas Brebner <douglas+mail@fang.demon.co.uk>).
	* Updated libexif to 0.5.11.
	* Other code improvements.

Version-0.2.23

	* Fixed clash bug of slideshow.
	* Plugged memory leak of JPEG loader.
	* Other minor fixes.

Version-0.2.22

	* Added automatic rotation by EXIF data.
	 (contributed from Frank Fischer <frank_fischer@gmx.de>. Thanks!)
	* Fixed detecting file name extension as case insensitive.
	 (Thanks! > Ricky Faulstich <Ricky@Faulstich.com>)
	* Fixed typo (Thanks! > Ricky Faulstich <Ricky@Faulstich.com>)

Version-0.2.21

	* Fixed compile error.

Version-0.2.20

	* Image loaders, I/O streamers, Image View and Thumbnail View Embders
          now are implemented as plugins.
	* Now GImageView can be compiled against linux-fb backend of Gtk+-2.0 by
	  "--with-gtk2=gtk+-linux-fb-2.0" configure opotion.
	* Merged Cygwin patch provided by Masahiro Sakai. Now GImageView can be
	  compiled on Cygwin.
	* Added some key binding to directory view on thumbnail window.
		CTRL + Cursor Left
		CTRL + Cursor Up: Change top directory to parent
		CTRL + Cursor Right
		CTRL + Cursor Down: Change top directory to selected
	* "Thumbnail 2" mode has been renamed to "Album" mode.
	* Added a key binding to "Album" mode.
		SHIFT + Cursor: select the fucesed image and open it.
	* Modified directory list preference to make it easy.
	* "Load thumbnails recursively in one tab" can be attached to mouse
	  button.
	* Now gimv doesn't zoom in by default when fit to frame automatically.
	* JPEG loader is added. Most of its codes are taken from libgnome-ui.
	  Creating JPEG thumbnails are much faster than GdkPixbuf.
	* Added "Slideshow (selected)" and "Slideshow (from the selected)".
	* Now you can override MPlayer options by
	  $(datadir)/gimageview/mplayerrc.
	* Enabled to play audio with visualizer
	  (Visualizer feature is supported by Xine view only).
	* Set focus to the suitable thumbnail when files are deleted.
	* Added rotation indicator in toolbar of image window.
	* Two new duplicates finders are added. One is "md5sum" and another one
	  is "File Size".
	* Clash bug of Xine view has been fixed.
	* Other minor fixes.
